{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794136025,"nonce":"XdiHNGkTyi2EFtjRsGlwUuWVHWI=","title":"rustybuzz is unmaintained (RUSTSEC-2026-0206): move blinc_text's shaper to harfrust","message":"RUSTSEC-2026-0206 marks rustybuzz unmaintained, with no patched version, and names harfrust, the HarfBuzz project's own Rust port, as the successor. The rustybuzz repository is archived.\n\nExposure here:\n- Direct: blinc_text depends on rustybuzz 0.20 (workspace dependency). Only shaper.rs uses it: Face::from_slice with the face index, a wght variation set through ttf_parser::Tag, UnicodeBuffer, rustybuzz::shape with and without features, and the Feature type.\n- Transitive, not ours to change: Cargo.lock also holds rustybuzz 0.18 through usvg 0.44, which blinc_svg uses for SVG text. That copy stays until usvg moves to harfrust.\n- CI: the Security Audit and Security Deny jobs run with continue-on-error, so they report it without failing. No deny.toml or audit.toml exists, so nothing ignores it yet.\n\nharfrust 0.15 is on crates.io. It is built on read-fonts and skrifa, not ttf-parser, so it is not a drop-in: the face, the shaper data, variation instances and the feature type differ.\n\nNeeded:\n- Replace the two shape paths in shaper.rs and the Feature type with harfrust, keeping ShapedText unchanged, including variable-font weight.\n- Compare shaped glyph ids, advances and clusters before and after on the existing shaping and layout tests plus a few cases: ligatures (Fira Code), a variable face at several weights, Arabic and Devanagari runs, emoji sequences.\n- Keep ttf-parser where blinc_text uses it for metrics and glyph lookup.\n- Decide on the usvg copy: wait for upstream, or add a deny.toml ignore for RUSTSEC-2026-0206 on that path with a note.","files":null}]}